#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:62
msgid "Procedure for finding and fixing bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:64
msgid ""
"When an AI assistant is used to find and fix bugs, it **MUST** follow at "
"least these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:67
msgid ""
"Before starting, read the whole process documentation listed above, as well "
"as any other document mentioned in the request. Do not rely on isolated "
"parts found by keyword search."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:70
msgid "Note the commit ID and Locate a bug as instructed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:71
msgid ""
"For any bug found that is not trivial, verify that it looks real by "
"attempting to create a reproducer to demonstrate it. Lacking it may cause "
"the report to be ignored, as many unverified bug reports sent to maintainers "
"happen to be invalid. Stop here if it finally looks wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:75
msgid ""
"Write a fix for the bug. This part is not optional: except in a few very "
"rare cases, an AI assistant able to find a bug is able to fix it. Note that "
"fixes written in the same session as used to find the bug will generally "
"lead to better and more accurate fixes as the LLM's reasoning context "
"remains present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:80
msgid ""
"Build and verify that the fix works either using the reproducer or by re-"
"running a complete analysis; drop any fix that doesn't work and try another "
"one. The fix must not add build warnings and must pass the checkpatch.pl "
"checks (see submitting-patches.rst)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:84
msgid ""
"Commit the working fix with a detailed message describing the problem, the "
"solution and a Fixes tag. Do not add a Signed-off-by tag, and add an "
"Assisted-by tag, as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:87
msgid ""
"Identify the maintainers and lists using scripts/get_maintainer.pl. "
"Documentation/process/security-bugs.rst shows how to do that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:89
msgid ""
"Indicate what could not be done. If the fix could not be built or tested, or "
"if no reproducer could be produced, say so explicitly: maintainers currently "
"waste too much time analyzing unverified reports and untested fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../process/coding-assistants.rst:92
msgid ""
"Read Documentation/process/threat-model.rst to determine whether the bug is "
"a vulnerability or a regular bug, and leave the result to the reporter for "
"review (the assistant must never send anything itself). Regular bugs are "
"submitted as described in Documentation/process/submitting-patches.rst, "
"vulnerabilities as described in Documentation/process/security-bugs.rst."
msgstr ""
